    --system-prompt for the built-in loop, --sample N --seed S for runs
    
    Two things harness researchers kept doing by hand. A prompt ablation was
    a fork of run.py; now it is a file and two runs, and every attempt
    records a hash of the system prompt it ran under so the arms cannot be
    confused after the fact. The nightly-15-of-40 pattern docs/ci.md
    recommends was left to shuf; now --sample 15 --seed 1 picks the same
    fifteen every night, ordered by sha first so the file's own order does
    not matter.
    
    Closes #34
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/groundhog/run.py b/groundhog/run.py
index 94db337..1f7b8da 100644
--- a/groundhog/run.py
+++ b/groundhog/run.py
@@ -97,6 +97,7 @@ class Attempt:
